messages:
maria (Docs): Quick check 111 I'm adding a small migration note for SOC2 customers switching from ad-hoc downloads to scheduled audit exports. Need a concise curl + node snippet showing tenant scoping, time-range, redact_level, retention_cutoff_ts, and export_ttl_seconds. Also need legal-approved copy that makes clear customers retain responsibility for exported copies (we provide short-lived links, not custody).

sam (Legal): Suggested line to include verbatim: "Exported audit datasets are snapshots of events at the time of export. Customers are responsible for downstream retention, deletion, and access controls of exported copies. Redwood issues short-lived export URLs and encrypted delivery; it does not assume custody or ongoing retention obligations for exported copies." Avoid words like "permanent" or "guarantee".

asha (Eng): Endpoints to show: POST /v1/audit/exports (body: tenant_id, start_ts, end_ts, redact_level: none|partial|full, mask_fields[], retention_cutoff_ts, export_ttl_seconds) and GET /v1/audit/exports/{id}/download. We also support schedule cron expressions for scheduled exports but keep the example simple.

troy (DevEx): For the example keep export_ttl_seconds low (3600) and show streaming to disk. For Node show a streaming pipeline that writes lines to file and a small note about backpressure.

lucy (Product): Call out KMS behavior: encrypted exports will be wrapped with customer KMS; clients may need to perform a unwrap/decrypt step after download. Add a placeholder link to KMS docs.

ci-bot: CI for branch docs/audit-export-scheduler queued by asha  status: success :rocket:

maria (Docs): Draft snippets below. I'll trim copy to fit the public guide and then tag legal/product for approval.

```bash
# create export (example)
curl -X POST "https://api.redwood.example/v1/audit/exports" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $REDWOOD_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "tenant_id": "blue-works",
    "start_ts": 1690848000,
    "end_ts": 1690934400,
    "redact_level": "partial",
    "mask_fields": ["email","phone"],
    "retention_cutoff_ts": 1688169600,
    "export_ttl_seconds": 3600
  }'

# download (stream to file)
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $REDWOOD_API_KEY" \
  "https://api.redwood.example/v1/audit/exports/EXPORT_ID/download" \
  --output blue-works-audit-2023-08-01.jsonl
```

```js
// node streaming example (axios + fs)
const fs = require('fs');
const axios = require('axios');
(async () => {
  const url = 'https://api.redwood.example/v1/audit/exports/EXPORT_ID/download';
  const resp = await axios.get(url, {
    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY}` },
    responseType: 'stream'
  });
  const out = fs.createWriteStream('blue-works-audit.jsonl');
  resp.data.pipe(out);
  out.on('finish', () => console.log('download complete'));
})();
```

sam (Legal): These snippets are fine. Please include this short paragraph in the migration note (exact wording): "Exported audit datasets are snapshots of events at the time of export. Customers are responsible for downstream retention, deletion, and access controls of exported copies. Redwood issues short-lived export URLs and encrypted delivery; it does not assume custody or ongoing retention obligations for exported copies."

maria (Docs): Will do. Also adding a short checklist:
- service account scopes: `audit:read`, `export:create` (optional: `kms:decrypt` for client-side unwrap)
- example export_ttl_seconds: 3600 (1 hour)
- migration tip: when scheduling exports, set retention_cutoff_ts to prevent exporting records older than your retention policy
- note: encrypted exports delivered via KMS will require client-side unwrap; binary attachments may be base64-encoded in JSONL

asha (Eng): Minor add: scheduled exports inherit tenant-level retention flags; if a record is under legal hold it may be omitted from exports depending on tenant policy.

maria (Docs): Thanks all  I'll land PR #489 and tag legal/product for final sign-off.
